      <div type="clause" n="6.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IIIEg">III Eg</ref> 6.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="6.1" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="202" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ gyf<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#IIIEg_6-1.lnote.oe.7-2"/> hwa<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="24" target="#IIIEg_6-1.lnote.oe.24"/> þon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> woh wyrce ⁊ utoðberste<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="25" target="#IIIEg_6-1.lnote.oe.25"/>, abere se borh þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he aberan scolde.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="26" target="#IIIEg_6-1.lnote.oe.26"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="6.1" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="202" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ gyf hwa þon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> woh wyrce ⁊ útætberste, abere se borh þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he aberan scolde.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="6.1" corresp="#wit-d"><pb n="202" ed="#liebermann"/>And gif hwa ðonne woh wirce ⁊ utaberste, abere se borh þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he beran scolde.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="6.1" corresp="#wit-g2"><pb n="203" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ gif hwa þonne woh wyrce ⁊ utætberste, abere se borh þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he beran scolde.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="6.1" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="203" ed="#liebermann"/>Et si quis iniuriam faciat et aufugiat, portet<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#IIIEg_6-1.lnote.oe.7"/> plegius quod ille portare debuerat.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="6.1" corresp="#wit-d"><pb n="26" ed="#robertson"/>⁊ gif hwa ðonne woh wirce ⁊ utaberste<ptr type="editorNote" n="5" target="#IIIEg_6-1.robnote.fn.5"/>, abere se borh þæt he beran<ptr type="editorNote" n="6" target="#IIIEg_6-1.robnote.fn.6"/> scolde.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="356" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And gyf hwa þonne woh wyrce and ut oðberste, abere se borh þæt he aberan scolde.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="203" ed="#liebermann"/>Und wenn einer dann Missethat verübt und entflieht<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IIIEg_6-1.lnote.de.1"/>, so trage der Bürge [Ersatz-<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IIIEg_6-1.lnote.de.2"/> und Strafgeld], was jener hätte tragen sollen.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And if anyone then does wrong and escapes, let the surety bear [the compensation and fine] that the other should have borne.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-d"><pb n="27" ed="#robertson"/>And if anyone does wrong and escapes<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IIIEg_6-1.robnote.n.1"/>, his surety shall incur what the other should have incurred<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#IIIEg_6-1.robnote.n.2"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="436" ed="#whitelock"/>And if anyone then commits a crime and escapes, the surety is to incur what he [the criminal] would have incurred.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="357" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And if anyone commits a crime and escapes, his surety shall suffer what he would have suffered.</ab>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIIEg_6-1.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">203</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">porte <hi rend="italic">MHk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">porte MHk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIIEg_6-1.lnote.oe.7-2" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">202</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">gif <hi rend="italic">So Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">gif So Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIIEg_6-1.lnote.oe.24" n="24" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">202</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt So</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in So</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIIEg_6-1.lnote.oe.25" n="25" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">202</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-bærste <hi rend="italic">So</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-bærste So</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIIEg_6-1.lnote.oe.26" n="26" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">202</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sculde <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sculde Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IIIEg_6-1.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">137</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Älteres <hi rend="italic">oð</hi>- wird auch sonst von jüngeren Texten durch <hi rend="italic">æt</hi>- ersetzt; <hi rend="italic">s. Wb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The older <hi rend="italic">oð</hi>- is replaced by <hi rend="italic">æt</hi>- in later texts elsewhere too; <hi rend="italic">see Wb</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IIIEg_6-1.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">137</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Nur den Ersatz nennt Ine 22. I Atr 1, 7. Zwar fällt dort Buss- und Strafgeld fort, da der Entflohene friedlos geworden; hier aber meint Eg offenbar alle Geldschuld, die der sich stellende Verbrecher selbst auf sich lüde. Den Bürgen trifft nur Geldverlust, nicht Leibesstrafe, noch auch, falls der Verbürgte Totschlag beging, Fehdegefahr. <hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Haftung 18</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Ine 22. I Atr 1, 7 mention only the restitution. There, it is true, compensation and fine fall away, since the fugitive has become an outlaw; but here Eg evidently means all the money liability that the criminal, had he presented himself, would himself have incurred. The surety suffers only loss of money, not corporal punishment, nor, if the man for whom he stood surety committed homicide, the danger of feud. <hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Haftung 18</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IIIEg_6-1.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">305</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. In. 22; <hi rend="italic">utoðberste</hi> (G) is the older form.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IIIEg_6-1.robnote.n.2" n="2" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">305</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">i.e.</hi> the payment of any money compensation due from the delinquent.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IIIEg_6-1.robnote.fn.5" n="5" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">26</biblScope></bibl><label>utaberste</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">utoðberste</hi> G, Ld; <hi rend="italic">utætberste</hi> A, G₂.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IIIEg_6-1.robnote.fn.6" n="6" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">26</biblScope></bibl><label>beran</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">aberan</hi> G, A, Ld.</seg></note>
      </div>
    </body>
